{%- comment -%}
  A customer-care page: a heading, a short intro, and a stack of headed
  paragraphs.

  ONE SECTION, TWO PAGES, built 2026-09-27 for Shipping & Delivery and Returns &
  Exchanges — the two footer entries that had been rendering as plain text since
  the footer copy landed because no page existed to link them to. They are the
  same shape (a policy, in sections, with a way to ask a human at the end), so
  they are one section with two templates rather than two sections that would
  drift apart the first time one got a design tweak.

  ⚠ WHAT IS ON RECORD AND WHAT IS NOT. The defaults in the two templates were
  generated on instruction — "coba lo generate lah page nya" — and they are
  deliberately built out of facts this repo already holds rather than out of
  plausible-sounding policy:

    on record   dispatch in 1–2 working days from Kota Bekasi (the product
                page's shipping line, live since 2026-09-22)
    on record   one free size exchange within 7 days (same line)
    on record   rates are calculated at checkout (the bag's own copy, and a
                platform constraint — see CLAUDE.md, Indonesian couriers quote
                during checkout through a RajaOngkir/Biteship app)
    on record   free shipping over Rp 750.000 (the announcement bar's default)
    NOT on record   which couriers, transit times, refund terms, who pays
                return postage, what happens to a damaged parcel

  Everything in the last row is written as "message the studio" rather than as a
  term, because a term nobody has set is an invented commitment and this repo
  refuses those. That is not padding — it is also how this studio actually
  operates: PRODUCT.md's customer evidence is full of shoppers describing the
  admin answering them directly. THE STUDIO SHOULD STILL SET REAL TERMS, and
  HANDOVER.md flags it.

  THE BLOCKS ARE `richtext`, NOT `textarea`, so a paragraph can carry a link —
  "message us on WhatsApp" is worth being a link on a page whose whole job is
  telling someone how to reach a human. A blank block renders its labelled
  placeholder at final size like every other empty slot here.

  NO PRICES, NO RATES, NO COURIER NAMES may be typed into these blocks. The bag
  says "Calculated at checkout" because Shopify is the only thing that knows,
  and a rate written here would be a second source that goes stale silently.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-content flex-col gap-block px-gutter pb-section pt-block-lg">
  <div data-reveal class="wl-measure flex flex-col gap-4">
    <span class="text-micro uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-ink-subtle">
      {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.eyebrow, label: 'eyebrow', inline: true %}
    </span>

    <h1 class="text-h1 leading-h1">
      {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.heading, label: 'heading', lines: 2 %}
    </h1>

    <p class="text-body leading-body text-ink-muted">
      {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.body, label: 'intro', lines: 2 %}
    </p>
  </div>

  {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
    <div class="flex flex-col divide-y divide-rule border-t border-rule">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Each item is a heading and its answer, in a two-column layout above
          `lg` so the eye can run down the headings alone. Below `lg` it stacks,
          because a 390px screen cannot hold two columns and a policy read on a
          phone is read in order anyway.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <section class="grid gap-3 py-7 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,2fr)] lg:gap-block" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          <h2 class="font-display text-h4 text-ink">
            {% render 'copy', value: block.settings.title, label: 'title' %}
          </h2>
          <div class="wl-measure text-body leading-body text-ink-body">
            {% render 'copy', value: block.settings.body, label: 'answer', lines: 3 %}
          </div>
        </section>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    The closing note is a section setting rather than a fourth block, because it
    is the one thing on this page that must not be reorderable: "still not sure?
    ask us" only works last.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if section.settings.footnote != blank -%}
    <div data-reveal class="rounded-md border border-border bg-canvas p-6 lg:p-8">
      <div class="wl-measure text-body leading-body text-ink-body">{{ section.settings.footnote }}</div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Customer care page",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A policy page: heading, intro, then one block per point. Do NOT type a shipping rate, a courier name or a transit time into any block. Shopify quotes rates at checkout and is the only thing that knows them, so a number written here is a second source that goes stale without anyone noticing."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Intro" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "footnote", "label": "Closing note", "info": "Sits in a card at the end of the page. It is a setting and not a block so that it always comes last." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "item",
      "name": "Point",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Heading" },
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "body", "label": "Answer" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Customer care page" }]
}
{% endschema %}
